  "agent": {
    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/charts/line-chart/v1`** (gate 16 — charts pack 3/4; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Props = showcase defaults. Internal `line-chart/internal/chrome/v1` rides base·int; alpine/line-chart/v2 already shipped base.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | not internal, not deprecated, primitive:true | confirm |\n| Gate | — | **base** |\n| Preview assets | committed set — default look unchanged at 1280×720 (caps bind only on overflow) | confirm |\n| Cover / Tutorial | cover BUILT this gate (draw-on starts near-blank; chart inlined flat above the band) | eyeball cover; tutorial needed? |\n\n**Pre-audit found + fixed 7:**\n1. **The CLI text-clip class, template-wide**: every chrome text cell is `fit:\"contain\"` — the app shrinks, the CLI CLIPS (the exact Make-vs-render gap alpine v2's textFits closed). At 360×640 the title/subtitle clipped BOTH edges, 12 x labels shredded into \"JaFebMarApr…\". Now script-aware width caps (title 0.66em, rest 0.62em) + floor ellipsis last resort.\n2. **Legend was wide-script blind** (flat 0.55em/char): Cyrillic legend labels clipped mid-word at EVERY canvas. textEmUnits widths + when the row would overflow its basis, font steps down then labels ellipsize to their squeezed cells.\n3. **X-label AUTOSKIP with widened cells** (chart.js behavior): when the pitch can't fit a label, every k-th shows and OWNS the skipped span — blanking alone left the shown label in its original narrow cell, still clipping. Shown labels keep full font.\n4. **Y-gutter AUTO-WIDTH**: the fixed 72px left pad clipped \"$9,850,000 USD\" ticks; when padding isn't explicit the gutter sizes to the longest formatted tick (explicit padding respected; font cap is the backstop).\n5. **Default y tick count now scales with plot height** (11 ticks overlapped below ~500px).\n6. **Area opacity rendered FULLY OPAQUE** — `color@0.2` is discarded by the inline-mask's coverage, so an area fill buried every series beneath it. Now a CONSTANT overlay.alpha (no per-frame expr — R6-safe; spec updated to assert no TIME-VARYING alpha).\n7. **Canvas color painted as a real base tile** — the known candidate 2026-08-06-template-invocation-bg-drop blacked the canvas + corner notches through the .mosaicx path (same workaround donut/v4 shipped at gate 15).\n\nAlso: debugLayout contract (6 textFits groups — title/subtitle/legend/y-tick/x-label/value-label; ALL text is literal so coverage is unconditional; checkLayout auto-flattens through the nested chrome child), tagged sources, cover.\n\n**Primitive-sense: KEEP primitive:true** — the canonical line-chart data-viz primitive.\n\nBattery 84/84 (baseline was feasibility-green but VISUALLY broken at small canvases — the stills tell it) + 84/84 final build, contract probe 14/14 defaults + 70/70 binding configs (Cyrillic, $-prefixed ticks, N=24 dense, dark+dashed+area), jest 34/34.",
    "question": "Default look verdict? Cover OK? Tutorial needed? primitive:true confirmed? Autoskip + auto-gutter look shifts acceptable? Then stress."
